I arrive at the office.
I go to my desk.
I put my laptop bag on the chair.
Then, I start my computer.
Today, I have a lot of work.
One piece of code is very difficult.
My colleague Rohan comes there.
"Good morning, Maya," Rohan says.
"Good morning, Rohan."
"How are you?" I ask.
"I am fine."
"Are you busy?" he asks.
"Yes, this new code is a little difficult," I say.
Rohan looks at my computer screen.
We both read that code together.
We discuss the code.
"There is a small mistake here," Rohan says.
He shows me that mistake.
I immediately correct that mistake.
Now my code works properly.
"Thank you, Rohan," I say happily.
We start our work again.
